WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.802 --> 00:00:03.010
STEPHANIE WONG: Today, we're
talking about reCAPTCHA,

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.340
self-service security
analytics, autonomous vehicles,

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.687
and Climate TRACE.

00:00:07.687 --> 00:00:10.270
I'm Stephanie Wong, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.840
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.830
ReCAPTCHA Enterprise is Google's
online fraud detection service

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.140
that leverages over a
decade of experience

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.280
defending the internet.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.410
ReCAPTCHA Enterprise
can be used to prevent

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.140
fraud and attacks
perpetrated by scripts,

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.940
bot software, or humans.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.250
As a part of our
continued investment here,

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.430
we're announcing Account
Defender in public preview.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.460
It's a new feature built into
reCAPTCHA Enterprise that

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.160
helps you determine if an
action aligns or deviates

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.650
from the account owner's
typical behavior.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.200
As more organizations
embrace the principles

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.600
of autonomic
security operations,

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.430
we continue to
research and develop

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.290
new initiatives
that can simplify

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.600
the adoption of
continuous detection

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.480
and continuous response
workflows for security

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.860
operations teams.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.010
To this end, we're excited to
announce Community Security

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.519
Analytics, a set of open source
queries and rules designed

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:06.890
for self-service security
analytics designed

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.790
to help detect common
cloud-based threats.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.150
As we continue to explore
climate solutions using machine

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.040
learning in our "People and
Planet" AI YouTube series,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.940
we have been blown away by
an amazing project called

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.080
Climate TRACE.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.850
It's a collaborative
data-sharing effort

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.090
across 50-plus organizations
with the intention of helping

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.450
the public, for free, to view
where carbon pollution is

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.820
emitted by country
and even by industry

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.640
in a meaningful and
visual way as a web app.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.350
Learn more and check out
the video in the blog.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.050
Cruise has been focused
on tackling city driving

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:44.920
since 2013, and with more than
3 million autonomous miles

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.960
under our belt,
we're getting closer

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.350
to delivering an all-electric
shared self-driving service.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:54.790
In January 2002, we reached
a major milestone-- members

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.670
of the public took their very
first fully driverless rides

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:58.840
in San Francisco.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.480
Developing an urban fleet
of fully autonomous vehicles

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.310
is an incredible challenge.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:06.160
To be successful, we needed
to build both the AV tech

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.620
that's out on the road
and the ecosystem of tools

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.479
our engineers use internally.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:13.217
Check out the blog for more.

00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:15.300
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.890
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.020
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.590
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.210
We'll see you in the cloud.

